## One proof run per state of the tree

A proof run is keyed by the tree it ran on — HEAD, the diff, and the contents of the
files git does not track yet:

```bash
echo "$(git rev-parse --short HEAD)-$({ git diff HEAD; git ls-files --others --exclude-standard; git ls-files --others --exclude-standard | git hash-object --stdin-paths; } | git hash-object --stdin | cut -c1-8)"
```

Run the proof commands once per key and append `<key> pass|fail <command>`
to `.work/proof.txt` (gitignored). A later step with the same key reads that
file instead of running them again; a different key runs them again.
